# Calendar event Supabase sync

**Status:** Implemented in app (Aug 2026). `SUPABASE_EVENTS.sql` **has been applied** (live). Do not treat “run events SQL” as a launch blocker.

## What shipped

- Bidirectional sync: push dirty locals → pull remote (last-`updatedAt`-wins) → orphan remote cleanup.
- Tables: `events`, `event_items` (with `sort_order`), `event_outfits`.
- Privacy: `visibility` (`private` / `friends` / `public`), **default private**; Create Event picker.
- Soft-delete → hard delete remote → local tombstone purge (with items/outfits).
- Incremental `SyncService.syncEventIfNeeded` on create/edit/delete/selection (background `Task`, gated on `enablesCloudSync`).
- Join upserts retry when linked item/outfit missing on server (`syncedAt` left nil).
- Pull only replaces joins when every remote FK resolves locally (avoids wiping links).

## Still deferred / separate

- Google Calendar import — out of scope.
- Friends/public **read** RLS + event Redress permission — see `calendar-event-privacy-redress-deferred.mdc` (visibility is stored; other-user calendar surfaces not wired).
- Other-user profile calendar tab — `other-user-profile-calendar-deferred.mdc`.

## Ops

- `SUPABASE_EVENTS.sql` already run on the project (Aug 2026).
- RLS remains owner-only manage (`SUPABASE_RLS_POLICIES.sql`); friends/public **read** is still deferred (`calendar-event-privacy-redress-deferred.mdc`).
